 -- TypeScipt(it is declarative code)

 --config files in Angular are responesible for converting TypeScipt to Javascript and helps in compilation( generally browser 
 do not support TypeScipt)

 --package.json files have dependencies
 --angular.json have configurations
 --src is the main folder which has main.ts(first file to execute when application is loaded),assets,html etc..
    (It is the folder where our main application logic will be written)

 --node modules contains all third part libraries on which Angular Application depend on  
 --styles.css->(for global styles)
 --gitignore -> It ensures that certain files or folders remain hidden  from git repository
 --index.html is the entry point of application while execution


To check Angular version 
 In Angular CLI enter :  ng version 

To install Angular@CLI globally
 In Angular CLI enter : npm i -g @angular/cli 